<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103249" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσᾰρεσκαίδεκα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσερ-</span></b> , οἱ, αἱ, τά,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fourteen</i>, the first
			part remaining unaltered even with a neut. Subst., as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτεα τεσσερεσκαίδεκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.86
				</span></i>
			; or with a gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέχρι τῶν τεσσαρεσκαίδεκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.</u>
					3.16
				</span></i>
			:—but sts. the first part changed its gender, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέσσαρα καὶ δέκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					12
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
